=== Naksa period (1967–1986) ===
During the 1967 [[Six-Day War]], hundreds of thousands of Palestinian refugees were driven from the West Bank, Gaza, and [[East Jerusalem]]. Most were driven into Jordan.{{sfnm |Masalha |2012 |1pp=13 and 128 |2a1=Abu-Lughod |2a2=Sa'di |2y=2007 |2p=19}} This has become known as ''[[1967 Palestinian exodus|al-Naksa]]'' (the "setback").{{sfnm |Manna |2013 |1p=86 |Jayyusi |2007 |2pp=109 and 115}} After the war, Israel [[Israeli occupation of the West Bank|occupied the West Bank]] and Gaza Strip.{{sfnm |1a1=Shenhav |1y=2019 |1p=49 |2a1=Bashir |2a2=Goldberg |2y=2018 |2p=7 |3a1=Rouhana |3a2=Sabbagh-Khoury |3y=2017 |3p=405 |4a1=Manna |4y=2013 |4pp=94-97 |5a1=Masalha |5y=2012 |5pp=168-169 |6a1=Morris |6y=2008 |6p=419 |7a1=Abu-Lughod |7a2=Sa'di |7y=2007 |7pp=3 and 19}}

