=== Since the First Intifada (1987–present) ===
The [[First Intifada]] began in 1987 and lasted until the 1993 [[Oslo Accords]].{{sfnm |Khalidi |2020 |1pp=164-199 |Manna |2013 |2p=99 n. 16 |Masalha |2012 |3p=75 |4a1=Lentin |4y=2010 |4p=88 |5a1=Abu-Lughod |5a2=Sa'di |5y=2007 |5pp=5 and 19}} The [[Second Intifada]] began in 2000.{{sfnm |1a1=Khalidi |1y=2020 |1pp=200-227 |2a1=Rouhana |2a2=Sabbagh-Khoury |2y=2014 |2p=15 |3a1=Manna |3y=2013 |3p=97 |4a1=Masalha |4y=2012 |4pp=75, 189-190 and 198-199 |5a1=Abu-Lughod |5a2=Sa'di |5y=2007 |5pp=3 and 19}} In 2005, Israel [[Israeli disengagement from Gaza|withdrew from Gaza]] and [[Blockade of the Gaza Strip|blockaded it]].{{sfnm |1a1=Bashir |1a2=Goldberg |1y=2018 |1p=1 |2a1=Khoury |2y=2018 |2p=xiv |3a1=Manna |3y=2013 |3p=97 and 99 n. 10 |4a1=Masalha |4y=2012 |4p=254}} In the West Bank and [[East Jerusalem]], Israel built the [[Israeli West Bank barrier]]{{sfnm |1a1=Abu-Lughod |1a2=Sa'di |1y=2007 |1p=23 |2a1=Jayyusi |2y=2007 |2pp=123}} and created [[Palestinian enclaves]].{{sfnm |Sayigh |2023 |1p=281 |Khoury |2018 |2p=xiv |Manna |2013 |3p=97 |Masalha |2012 |4p=47 and 254}}

In 2011, Israel passed the [[Nakba Law]], which denies government funding to institutions that commemorate the Nakba.{{sfnm |1a1=Shenhav |1y=2019 |1p=49 |2a1=Bashir |2a2=Goldberg |2y=2018 |2p=2 |3a1=Rouhana |3a2=Sabbagh-Khoury |3y=2017 |3p=418 and 423 |4a1=Rashed |4a2=Short |4a3=Docker |4y=2014 |4pp=16-17 |5a1=Rouhana |5a2=Sabbagh-Khoury |5y=2014 |5p=14}}

